From: clawd20130 <clawd20130@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 16:46:20 +0900
Subject: Screencast: another RGB format for DMA-BUF frames when the allocator
 cannot make the source's

The stream offered DMA-BUF frames only in the source's format (or ARGB8888) and fell back to memfd
when that one could not be allocated. The Android host's buffer lease makes only RGBA-ordered
buffers (ABGR8888/XBGR8888), and the output is ARGB8888: every screencast went through memfd, read
back by KWin and uploaded again by the consumer. At 1080x2400 and 60 fps the screen recorder's GL
thread spent about 0.4 of a core copying those frames into textures (docs/108). Rendering into the
stream's buffer converts between formats at no cost, so the other 8-bit RGB formats are tried
before memfd.

Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-04
X-Rungic-Status: Pending [generic: screencast allocators that make a subset of the renderer's formats]
X-Rungic-Tests: L3:recording.quicksetting
X-Rungic-Docs: docs/108
Origin: vendor
---
 src/plugins/screencast/screencaststream.cpp | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/plugins/screencast/screencaststream.cpp b/src/plugins/screencast/screencaststream.cpp
index 9d99293..1533ddb 100644
--- a/src/plugins/screencast/screencaststream.cpp
+++ b/src/plugins/screencast/screencaststream.cpp
@@ -426,6 +426,24 @@ bool ScreenCastStream::createStream()
         m_modifiers = *itModifiers;
     }
     m_hasDmaBuf = testCreateDmaBuf(m_resolution, m_drmFormat, m_modifiers).has_value();
+    // The allocator may not make every format the renderer can draw: the Android host leases only
+    // RGBA-ordered buffers (ABGR8888/XBGR8888), not the output's ARGB8888. Rendering converts for
+    // free, so try another 8-bit RGB format before resorting to memfd (copied by the CPU on both
+    // sides of the stream).
+    for (const uint32_t format : {DRM_FORMAT_ABGR8888, DRM_FORMAT_XBGR8888, DRM_FORMAT_ARGB8888, DRM_FORMAT_XRGB8888}) {
+        if (m_hasDmaBuf) {
+            break;
+        }
+        const auto it = supported.constFind(format);
+        if (format == m_drmFormat || it == supported.constEnd()) {
+            continue;
+        }
+        if (testCreateDmaBuf(m_resolution, format, *it).has_value()) {
+            m_drmFormat = format;
+            m_modifiers = *it;
+            m_hasDmaBuf = true;
+        }
+    }
 
     char buffer[2048];
     QList<const spa_pod *> params = buildFormats(false, buffer);
